 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Six independent inverters. Each output nY goes HIGH when its input nA is LOW and LOW when nA is HIGH."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Schmitt-trigger inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each input switches at VT+ on a rising edge and at the lower VT- on a falling edge; the gap between them is the hysteresis VH. A slow or noisy input therefore gives a clean, fast output edge, and there is no limit on input rise and fall time."
  },
  {
   "topic": "HC and HCT",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 74HC14 works from 2.0 V to 6.0 V. The 74HCT14 works from 4.5 V to 5.5 V with lowered thresholds (VT+ 1.9 V max, VT- 0.5 V min at VCC = 4.5 V) so it accepts TTL levels. An HCT input held at VCC - 2.1 V draws an extra ΔICC of up to 108 µA at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input clamp diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs have clamp diodes; with a series current-limiting resistor an input can be driven from a voltage above VCC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply current during transitions",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Supply current rises while the input sits partway between GND and VCC: at VCC = 6.0 V the 74HC typically peaks near 0.84 mA. Slow input rise and fall times add dissipation, given by the Padd equation and the ΔICC(AV) curves."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Robustness",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Latch-up: above 100 mA, JESD 78 Class II Level B. ESD: above 2000 V HBM (JS-001 class 2) and above 1000 V CDM (JS-002 class C3). Complies with JESD8C (2.7 V to 3.6 V) and JESD7A (2.0 V to 6.0 V)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Limits are given for two ambient ranges: -40 °C to +85 °C and -40 °C to +125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Wave and pulse shaping, astable multivibrators and monostable multivibrators."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching measurement",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Delays are timed between the VM crossings of input and output; transition times between the 10 % and 90 % points of the output. The 74HC14 is driven GND to VCC with VM = 0.5 × VCC; the 74HCT14 is driven GND to 3.0 V with VM = 1.3 V. Input edges are 6.0 ns."
  }
 ],
